{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups","id":1233079,"title":"Susceptibility of Other Sups","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-07T13:57:35-07:00","id":1233079,"title":"Susceptibility of Other Sups","content":"Two quick questions:<br /> 1. Can mages be ghouls or are they immune?<br /> 2. Is a Werewolf susceptible to a blood bind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20755-seph038","name":"Seph038","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T14:02:29-07:00","id":1233080,"title":"","content":"Supernaturals cannot be ghouls. No mages, werewolves, changelings, etc.<br /> <br /> Everyone is susceptible to blood bonds. Werewolves, mages, changelings, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T14:23:21-07:00","id":1233083,"title":"","content":"Mages can't be ghouls, but they are susceptible to blood bonds. Although being mages, they have more ways to break them than other supernatural beings do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T14:37:50-07:00","id":1233085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233083#post1233083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can't be ghouls, but they are susceptible to blood bonds. Although being mages, they have more ways to break them than other supernatural beings do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please make some example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T14:53:42-07:00","id":1233087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233085#post1233085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you please make some example?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can likely scour the bond from their own patterns, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T17:17:23-07:00","id":1233116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233087#post1233087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can likely scour the bond from their own patterns, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not likely according to the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T17:37:13-07:00","id":1233119,"title":"","content":"Pattern Restoration lets you remove a Mental Condition (no Beat) as an instant action, but blood bonds do sidestep that by not being Conditions, technically. I guess it depends on the limits. Could you remove a headache or mental exhaustion, even if you don't have a condition for it?<br /> <br /> Using Arcana you'd probably need Space magic to cut the sympathetic ties, but could use easier things in Mind or Space to put them on hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-07-2018, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T01:14:31-07:00","id":1233154,"title":"","content":"All supernaturals are subject to the blood bond (but not ghouling), except Demons only are when they're in a Cover; you can't blood bond all of a Demon, just a Cover, per the Storyteller's guide.<br /> <br /> As for Mages, I think it's previously been stated Mind 2 can suppress the emotional pull of a Blood Bond, and Mind 5 or Space 5 can remove it entirely. It's not a condition, so can't be scoured (I believe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:26:48-07:00","id":1233173,"title":"","content":"was told when STing a Princess game in first edition that no supernatural but vamps was susceptible to a blood bond<br /> <br /> Did we Misread thjings? or were rules changed in 2nd edition jkust curious? <br /> <br /> Ghouled Mages and &quot;Abominations&quot; were dedliberately excised as possibletys in Chronicles of Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone loves to hate Sam Haight, is the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:57:04-07:00","id":1233179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233173#post1233173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">was told when STing a Princess game in first edition that no supernatural but vamps was susceptible to a blood bond<br /> <br /> Did we Misread thjings? or were rules changed in 2nd edition jkust curious? <br /> <br /> Ghouled Mages and &amp;quot;Abominations&amp;quot; were dedliberately excised as possibletys in Chronicles of Darkness&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone loves to hate Sam Haight, is the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the FAQ: Can werewolves, mages, demons, and other monsters be blood bonded?<br /> Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T05:58:42-07:00","id":1233180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233173#post1233173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">was told when STing a Princess game in first edition that no supernatural but vamps was susceptible to a blood bond<br /> <br /> Did we Misread thjings? or were rules changed in 2nd edition jkust curious?<br /> <br /> Ghouled Mages and &quot;Abominations&quot; were dedliberately excised as possibletys in Chronicles of Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone loves to hate Sam Haight, is the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were confusing blood bond with ghouling. They're different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T15:32:35-07:00","id":1233291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1233079-susceptibility-of-other-sups?p=1233085#post1233085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you please make some example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way I could think of to actually break the bond would be with an unraveling Death effect (since I believe vampiric powers fall under Death) or a 4th level bond-breaking Fate effect. Mind and probably Life at level 2 could temporarily suppress the effects of a bond.. Spirit could likely get hold of something that could destroy the bond, but it may be easier said than done to find and bind the appropriate spirit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:07:46-07:00","id":1237127,"title":"","content":"With regard to mages breaking the bond, there is more than one way to skin that cat in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As a power of the undead, Death could unravel it or prevent it.<br /> <br /> As a mind affecting power, Mind could unravel it or prevent it.<br /> <br /> As vitae that is ingested, Life could prevent it being absorbed and having any effect, good or bad.<br /> <br /> As a fluid (vitae), Matter could also prevent it from being absorbed, or if the mage has enough dots, just destroy the vitae before absorption or even ingestion. I would probably rule that Death would need to be used in conjunction to destroy it.<br /> <br /> Much like a geas, Fate would be able to destroy the bond. At least I think so.<br /> <br /> A spirit could be summoned with Spirit to break the bond. But I think the effort and price for such a task would not be worth it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that Prime would have much effect, and I don't think Space would do the trick either as I believe that the blood bond does not rely on sympathetic ties.<br /> <br /> However, the only surefire way to avoid the blood bond in my opinion would be to prevent the ingestion or absorption of the vitae. I believe that once the bond is in place, any magic used to break it would be subject to a Clash of Wills. Any such clash would be dependent on the power of the mage compared to the power of the vampire.<br /> <br /> So a noob mage is in deep doo doo if Dracula slips him a mickey, and conversely, Merlin will laugh at some newly turned fanger trying to bond him.<br /> <br /> Other splats have ways of breaking the bond, but the question I would pose is would they be aware of the blood bond? And if so, would they want to break their love for their precious? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}